
This folder contains the isoconfigurational trajectories of the KA2D model. The model has been developed and is described in reference:

Title: Predicting dynamic heterogeneity in glass-forming liquids by physics-inspired machine learning
Authors: G. Jung, G. Biroli, and L. Berthier 
Journal: Phyical Review Letters 130, 238202 (2023)
DOI: 10.1103/PhysRevLett.130.238202

The ".tar.xz" file contains data in the numpy .npz format, in exactly the same way as the data of Hayato Shiba for the KA model:

https://github.com/h3-Open-BDEC/pyg_botan

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

T0.30:

There are 20 isoconfigurational trajectories for each of the 3000 different structures (separated into a training and a testing set). The trajectories consists of six time stamps:
tc01: 0.11
tc02: 1.25
tc03: 14.14
tc04: 158.74
tc05: 1781.79
tc06: 20000

The format of the files is: N1290T0.30_{STRUCT}_tc{TIME}.npz where STRUCT denotes the index of the structure (1 - 3000) and TIME the time index as described above.

Each array contains the following information:

box: box length (=32.8962)
types: the type of each particle (1,2,3)
initial_positions: the initial positions of each particle in the structure (same for all tc)
positions: the positions of each particle after time scale tc. The array has a shape (20,1290,2) for the 20 isoconfigurational trajectories.

The structural relaxation time is tau_alpha=2200.

